 The registration is authoritative: covered-class climb is crash-free in at least 90% of seeds; hidden-class first-year crashes are at most two per CCD in at least 90%; maximum overshoot is at most one count in at least 95% and never more than three; median days within one count of true safe is at most 90; after two years on the stock-background scenario at least 90% keep converged depth minus one; fixed caps need at most seven promotions per CCD. Each criterion is evaluated per scenario using each seed's worst CCD, never pooled. Every censored or nonconverged run stays in the denominator, with infinite convergence time; partial counts cannot earn a pass. The committed registration describes applicable scenarios and exact empirical fractions. A failed score is an owner decision, not a reason to relax thresholds.
 
+#### Simulation-only B′ comparator
+
+`--policy ruleset13-bprime --slope <1.5|2.0>` selects a diagnostic alternative to
+Ruleset 13's cap and filler, not the shipped policy and never a gate pass.
+Only the simulation runner enables the tuner's default-off `sim-bprime` feature;
+the shipped `togi` package does not enable it. Normal state construction and
+deserialization always select the specified policy A. B′ cannot be selected by
+configuration, a journal, or a state snapshot.
+
+B′ pools each compatible isolated mapping class's observations across offsets
+in one slope-aware Poisson likelihood. At reference offset x, let
+`E_x = Σ T_i exp(beta*(x-o_i))` and `K = Σ k_i`; its rate upper endpoint is
+`chi_square_quantile(0.95, 2(K+1))/(2 E_x)`. The existing measured/fallback slope,
+CCD count, λ*, edge margin, qualification, night shares and daily rules stay
+unchanged. This is not the minimum of separate rate bounds.
+
+For each launch, `T_i = max(actual_seconds - 600, 0)/3600`; remove onset before
+aggregation. Short launches supply no sustained-day survival information.
+Failures still count, even before onset, with only their actual stopped
+exposure, never an intended-duration tail. Counting pre-onset failures against
+the post-onset rate is conservative rather than a claim of a literal
+onset-only generative model. Every class without an adequate positive-time
+mapping launch remains explicitly uncovered. Intended duration stays part of
+class identity; breadth cells do not stand in for long cells.
+
+The filler retains the specified CCD selection and rotation, but runs
+1,800-second isolated mapping cells at the deepest admissible signed offset
+`min(U+5, 0)`, rather than S−1. This is the only changed trial duration; ordinary
+mapping and qualification matrices are unchanged. This comparator must collect
+real post-onset time, since the ordinary mapping cells last only 90–120 seconds.
+
+The 95% endpoint is a fixed-look modeling calculation, **not an exact adaptive
+confidence interval**: offsets, exposure allocation and the measured slope
+depend on accumulated evidence. Neither B′ nor A demonstrates a rare-event
+guarantee on hardware. Reduced development-seed reads are exploratory and do
+not replace the preregistered full development and holdout gates.
+
 ### Historical gates
 
 The Ruleset 9 gate is defined by [ADR 0038](adr/0038-self-sufficient-cores.md) and [#105](https://github.com/shgew/togi/issues/105); [ADR 0040](adr/0040-located-hunts.md) records the Ruleset 10 gate. The [Ruleset 11 archive](../tools/bench/gates/ruleset-11/) holds its suite, baseline, candidate and scored report. These are historical records, not current-anchor measurements. The bench no longer judges any session-suite gate, and the archive is pinned by hash in the bench's tests.
